## String Basics

String is an object that stores a sequence of characters. It is *immutable*.

java
String s = "Java";
s.length();          // 4
s.charAt(0);         // 'J'
s.substring(1, 3);   // "av"
s.indexOf('v');      // 2
s.toUpperCase();     // "JAVA"
s.equals("Java");    // true
"a,b,c".split(",");  // ["a","b","c"]


## String Pool

java
String a = "Java";
String b = "Java";
String c = new String("Java");
a == b;        // true  (same pool object)
a == c;        // false (different object)
a.equals(c);   // true  (same content)


